#!/usr/bin/env python3
# session-open -- deterministic session BIRTH primitive (DGN session-lifecycle
# determinism). The symmetric partner of session-closeout (death).
#
# WHY (root fix, replaces the reverted set-add first-set bolt-on):
#   workouts.session_type_id is the CANONICAL SoT for a session's rotation day --
#   session-cursor, rx-calc rotation inference, and set-table all read the day
#   from it. Today the workouts row is born UNTAGGED (session_type_id NULL) at
#   SESSION_START (the model calls `kit_life.sh workout-add`) and is only tagged
#   at session-closeout, which is skippable. An untagged session causes:
#     - the wrap-up card deriving its label from muscle display ("가슴") instead
#       of the rotation code (앞A)  [batch #19],
#     - rx-calc seeing an untagged latest session -> provisional -> wrong-day
#       prescriptions / weight:null,
#     - a non-deterministic close  [batch #20].
#   session-open tags the row at BIRTH so the code is available from the first
#   moment, killing the untagged-session class of bugs at the root.
#
# WHAT (atomic session birth, idempotent):
#   (a) create/reconcile the workouts row by CALLING `kit_life.sh workout-add`
#       (framework -- preserves DGN-231 reconcile-before-write on (date, 대분류)
#       and every workout-add side effect, e.g. the card-followup hook). We do
#       NOT raw-insert.
#   (b) tag session_type_id immediately via the ENCAPSULATED canonical write
#       (session-closeout.tag_session_type, birth_only=True -- never clobbers an
#       existing tag). The day source is rx-calc's AUTHORITATIVE rotation_day +
#       session_class; we NEVER re-derive the day (session_class = rx-calc SoT).
#       regular -> rotation_day's session_type_id; makeup -> 보충 (never a
#       rotation type). If rx-calc's rotation is PROVISIONAL, the start-tag is
#       SKIPPED (leave NULL for closeout to tag authoritatively -- do not launder
#       an unconfirmed guess into a confirmed anchor).
#   (c) set the active-session marker (session-cursor.marker_write).
#
# Idempotency + safety:
#   - workout-add's own DGN-231 (date, 근력) reconcile means a second open on the
#     same day returns the EXISTING row (no double-create). We capture that id.
#   - birth_only tag never overwrites an existing tag (manual / closeout / a
#     prior open).
#   - STALE marker: if a marker for a DIFFERENT session is active when we open a
#     new one, we clear it (the new session's marker replaces it). A stuck marker
#     from a prior day can never survive an open. We report the takeover.
#   - best-effort tag / marker: a TAG failure alone must NOT fail the row+marker
#     creation (mirrors set-add's marker self-heal). The row is the critical
#     path; the tag and marker are best-effort layered on top.
#
# SAME-DAY 2ND SESSION (2026-08-20 mock-session incident, root fix):
#   workout-add's DGN-231 reconcile matches on (date, 근력) and returns the
#   EXISTING row for today. When today's row is ALREADY CLOSED (session-closeout
#   has run: the .session-closed tombstone holds it AND it is tagged), a plain
#   open would (1) reuse the CLOSED row, (2) skip the birth tag under the
#   no-clobber guard (leaving the OLD rotation code, e.g. 앞B), and (3) point
#   .active-session at a CLOSED session id -- a closed-but-active contradiction
#   that then desyncs the rotation calc (set-table computes "next = 뒷B" but the
#   reused row still reads 앞B). Fix: when today's reconciled row is closed, force
#   a BRAND-NEW row (`workout-add --new`, DGN-231 bypass) tagged at birth with the
#   AUTHORITATIVE next rotation day, and surface an overtraining note. We never
#   hard-block a 2nd session (owner may legitimately double up / mock-test) and we
#   never point the active marker at a closed id.
#
# Usage:
#   session-open [--date YYYY-MM-DD] [--db PATH] [--program PATH]
#                [--marker PATH] [--subtype CODE] [--minutes N] [--kcal N]
#                [--note TEXT] [--dry-run]
#     date defaults to today (KST). subtype defaults to the resolved rotation
#     code (or "보충" for a makeup session). rotation_day / session_class are
#     always taken from rx-calc (authoritative); they are never passed in.
#
# stdout (machine-parseable, one key=value block):
#   OPENED session_id=<id> created=<yes|existing> session_class=<regular|makeup>
#     rotation_day=<code> tag=<applied|skipped_provisional|skip_clobber|failed>
#     marker=<set|takeover|failed> ... taxonomy=<seeded|unseeded|partial|...>
#     install=<complete|incomplete:N>
#     us_step=<ok|synced:N[,unresolved:N]|collision|failed>  (G17 reconcile)
#     resumed=<yes|no>  yes = this open re-attached to today's LIVE session
#                       (the marker named it); nothing was forked
#   or ERROR <reason> on a hard failure (workout-add could not create the row).
#   CARE <n> line(s) ... + the indented lines, when the card carries `care:`
#     (the model says them verbatim at session start).
#
# INSTALL-COMPLETENESS ANNOUNCEMENT (2026-09-12). `health_taxonomy_seed.py --apply` is this
# pack's MANUAL post-install step and the only place it was written down was
# service/health/README.md -- which is not a caller, the same finding
# session-ensure.sh already carries for this script. An unseeded instance does
# not fail: it prescribes UNROUNDED weights with no empty-bar ramp, quietly.
# Session BIRTH is the one code path no session can skip, so the state is probed
# here, once per session, and announced on BOTH channels -- taxonomy= and
# install= keys in the machine-parseable block, and an INSTALL-GAP prose block
# addressed to the session agent (same vehicle as the START_CARD / NOTE lines
# below it). The same probe covers the three SoT files (prep.yaml /
# stretch-matrix.md / gym-layout.md) that ship as TEMPLATES and that no install
# lane places -- see install_gaps() for why two of them must never be
# auto-copied.
# It ANNOUNCES, it does not block: the workouts row is the critical path every
# later set-add hangs off, and a projection-config defect must not be able to
# suppress it. Refusing to PRESCRIBE is ax-project's job (exit 3) and it does.
#
# Exit codes:
#   0 = session open (row exists + marker handled; tag best-effort)
#   1 = hard error (workout-add failed / rx-calc unusable / bad args)
#
# Reuse (ladder): kit_life.sh workout-add (row + DGN-231 + hooks), rx-calc
# select_rotation_day/verdict (authoritative day + class), session-closeout
# tag_session_type (canonical tag write), session-cursor marker_* (active gate).
# stdlib only. ASCII source (Korean literals only where user-visible strings are
# unavoidable -- rotation codes come from the DB, not hardcoded).

